# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FreshNow — what never goes into git.
#
# Two reasons a file is listed here:
#   1. CONFIDENTIAL — keys, passwords, tokens, employee data, database dumps.
#      Once pushed, a secret must be treated as leaked and rotated; deleting it
#      in a later commit does not remove it from history.
#   2. NOT NEEDED TO RUN THE SYSTEM — build output, caches, logs, local tool
#      state. Every one of these is regenerated by `pnpm install` / a build / a run.
#
# If you need a file that matches a pattern below in the repo, add a specific
# `!path` exception with a comment saying why — do not delete the pattern.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Environment & secrets — NEVER commit real keys ──────────────────────────
# Every .env variant (.env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.staging, …) is
# ignored. Only the documented template with placeholder values is tracked.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
# Local credentials notes (dashboard logins) — see CREDENTIALS.local.md
*.local.md
CREDENTIALS*
!CREDENTIALS.example.md
# Private keys, certificates, keystores (TLS, SSH, VAPID, service accounts)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
*.csr
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets/
*.secret
*.secrets
service-account*.json
*-credentials.json
credentials.json
# Web push VAPID key pairs, if ever written to a file instead of .env
vapid*.json

# ── Database dumps, backups, exports (contain employee data) ─────────────────
*.dump
*.backup
*.bak
*.sql.gz
*.sql.zst
backups/
dumps/
exports/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# Redis persistence (snapshots and append-only files hold queued jobs and payloads)
*.rdb
*.aof
appendonlydir/

# ── Real company data handed over for analysis (TASK-055) ────────────────────
# WhatsApp exports carry staff phone numbers and photos; Televend exports carry
# employee names and machine sales; screenshots show the Televend account. The
# repository is PUBLIC (G114) — none of this may ever be pushed. Files stay where
# the user put them; these patterns only keep them out of git.
private-data/
data-televend/
CASH COLLECTION DAILY VENDING/
Warehouse stocks/
Freshnow Service Team*/
# Later WhatsApp handovers, folder by date ("whatsapp chat 19-10-2026", "16-10").
whatsapp chat */
16-10/
machines category wise/
hemanth task logging*.png
# Televend export files dropped anywhere else (event list, refill log, machine
# list, history log) — the file-import transport reads them from private-data/.
event_list*.xls
refill_log*.csv
VendingMachines*.xlsx
History_log*.xlsx
# Supabase Studio saves ad-hoc SQL here; it can hold real query results.
supabase/snippets/

# ── Supabase CLI local state (regenerated by `npx supabase start`) ──────────
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.env
supabase/volumes/
supabase/**/.env

# ── Caddy runtime data (issued certificates, ACME account keys) ─────────────
caddy_data/
caddy_config/
.caddy/

# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.tgz

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Next.js / Vite (dashboard)
packages/dashboard/.next/
packages/dashboard/out/
.vite/
.turbo/

# ── Test output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
blob-report/

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Runtime data: uploads, voice assets, local models (Tasks 016/017) ──────
data/
uploads/
models/
tmp/
.tmp/

# ── Caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.parcel-cache/

# ── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Claude Code: personal settings (the shared .claude/ config stays tracked) ─
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Reference PDFs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# freshnow/opt-COO*.pdf are "Print to PDF" copies of the markdown research in
# freshnow/*.md (~14.8 MB of duplicate binary). The markdown is the source.
freshnow/*.pdf
